# THE INPUT FILE for research-only dependencies. Edit THIS, never
# requirements-research.txt, which is GENERATED and constrained by the serving
# lock exactly as requirements-evidence.txt is.
#
# Installed on a research machine only: NOT by Render, NOT by the daily or
# weekly jobs. Install with
#
#     pip install -r requirements.txt -r requirements-evidence.txt -r requirements-research.txt
#
# Found 2026-09-21 by building an environment from the locks alone: every
# research tool reads panel_cache.parquet through pandas.read_parquet, which
# needs a parquet engine, and none was declared anywhere - the numbers in docs/
# were produced with the pyarrow that happened to be installed. pandas 3 also
# backs its default string dtype with pyarrow WHEN IT IS PRESENT, so this is
# not only an I/O dependency.
-c requirements.txt

pyarrow
